NAME: Vincenzo Macri'
SOAPBOX: Yaesu FT-950, MicroHam Microkeyr II, SPE Expert 1.3K-FA, and vertical antenna for 40, 20, 15, and 10 meters (but 10 meters is off limits for now!). Almost 24 hours of pure fun in my first RTTY contest I spent the first part in S&P searching for the most interesting multipliers, managing to connect most of them, and from early afternoon until Sunday evening I switched to RUN to increase the number of QSOs. I then concluded Sunday evening in S&P on 40 meters, searching for more multipliers. Not having a beam antenna seemed like the best strategy, and I'm satisfied with the result. I had some difficulties with the way many stations structure their QSOs, which sometimes doesn't help them manage data and pileups correctly. Finally, thanks to everyone who connected me.
SOAPBOX: 73 by Vincenzo IT9AQR
CREATED-BY: QARTest 15.8.1
